# SDIT Fajar — Cursor Rules & Code Instructions

# Core Principles
- Strictly adhere to Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript strict mode, and Tailwind CSS 4.
- NEVER use TypeScript `any`. All interfaces/types must live in `@/types/`.
- UI Design Concept: Minimalist Craft & Design Engineering (inspired by https://jakub.kr/).
  - Use Shadcn UI (Radix primitives) + Tailwind CSS 4 + Lucide React + Hugeicons React.
  - DO NOT use Claymorphism or Bento Grid styles.
  - ALL data tables MUST implement Zebra Cross styling (alternating row backgrounds `even:bg-muted/25`) with crisp borders.
  - UI copy must be in Bahasa Indonesia. Code/comments in clean English.

# Role & Authentication Rules
- Exact 5 roles: `super_admin`, `admin`, `guru`, `murid`, `wali_murid`. NEVER hallucinate other roles.
- Teacher positions (`kepala_sekolah`, `wali_kelas`, `bendahara`, `koordinator_tahfidz`, `pustakawan`, `operator`) are POSITIONS under role `guru`, not separate roles.
- Murid logs in using NIS and default birthdate password (`tempatddmmyyyy`), with required first-time password reset.
- ONLY `wali_murid` can initiate payments for their linked children via Midtrans Snap Popup Modal.
- Receipt generated as print-friendly clean web receipt with `@media print`.

# PPDB Online Staging Flow
- New applicant data is stored in the dedicated staging table `registrations`.
- Only promoted to `students` and given credentials after admin approval.

# Scope Exclusions
- Internal Chat / Real-time messaging feature is EXPLICITLY REMOVED from the system. Do not create chat tables, endpoints, or UI components.

# Security & Data Integrity
- Supabase RLS is mandatory for all tables.
- All client mutations must go through Next.js Server Actions with Zod schema validation.
- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` to client components.
- Midtrans webhook must strictly verify SHA512 signature keys before updating invoice statuses.
